   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Speed Lines\n\nComic-style motion streaks: a squashing ball leaves a trail as it lands, or rays rush out from a focus point.\n\nCategory: shapes. Length: 2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Something lands, zips in or snaps into focus and needs comic-style motion lines to sell the speed.\n- A hook, reveal or punchline needs radiating focus lines.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A calm, polished product tone is needed: speed lines read as playful and loud.\n- The moving object is complex content: the trail mode draws a plain ball.\n\nVariables:\n- mode (enum): Mode, default \"trail\"\n- from_x (number, -1-2): From X, default -0.25\n- from_y (number, -1-2): From Y, default 0.5\n- x (number, 0-1): X, default 0.5\n- y (number, 0-1): Y, default 0.5\n- count (number, 3-32): Lines, default 12\n- weight (number, 1-8): Weight, default 2\n- spread (number, 16-320): Spread, default 96\n- duration (number, 6-40): Travel frames, default 14\n- bounce (number, 0-1): Bounce, default 0.5\n- squash (number, 0-1): Squash, default 0.5\n- color (color): Line color, default \"#ffffff\"\n- seed (number, 1-99): Seed, default 1\n- delay (number, 0-60): Delay, default 0\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
